WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.270
- You've probably heard about

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.040
some of these bizarre legal defenses.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.700
The Twinkie Defense, what
could that possibly mean?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.470
Or if you've been on Reddit
you might have engaged

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.250
in a thought experiment
about what would happen

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.070
if one of two identical
twins committed a murder.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.730
They look exactly the same as their twin

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.420
and they share the same DNA.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.840
Well, the thing is these legal defenses

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.830
have actually been made, and
some were actually successful.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.700
Well, sort of successful.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.160
It depends on who you ask it. Partially...

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.490
Look, the law is complicated,

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.134
I don't know what to tell you, but...

00:00:29.134 --> 00:00:31.967
(cheerful music)

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.520
So stop me if you've heard this one.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.880
DMX, the rapper, plays
one of his songs in court

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.420
and receives a reduced sentence.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.870
Well, this actually happened.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.550
In April of 2021, the
world lost Earl Simmons,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.400
better known as the stage name DMX.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.430
A successful rapper,
songwriter, and actor,

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.940
DMX undoubtedly had
tremendous impact on music

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:49.870
and pop culture.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.410
But as often the case for entertainers,

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.720
with fame and fortune follows addiction

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.200
and a litany of legal troubles.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.050
And since 1986, DMX has
been jailed 30 times

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.270
for a variety of offenses,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.910
including robbery, assault,
carjacking, drug possession,

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.230
pretending to be a federal
agent, and tax evasion.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.730
But the reason we are
talking about DMX today

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.580
is for the unique defense
offered by X's attorneys

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.890
at his sentencing
hearing for his tax case.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.830
And in what sounds like a contrived plot

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.370
to an '80s movie no one actually saw,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:21.359
the day was saved in part
thanks to the power of hip hop.

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:23.569
♪ It's true I got the bars like candy ♪

00:01:23.569 --> 00:01:24.709
♪ But spitting verse like me ♪

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:26.659
♪ Will get you all up in the Grammy ♪

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:27.492
(record screeching)

00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:30.780
- No, no, not like that.
Definitely not like that.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.960
But in July of 2017, federal
prosecutors charged DMX

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.730
with 14 counts of tax fraud.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.010
The government alleged
the DMX owed 1.7 million

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.970
in unpaid taxes from income
earned between 2002 and 2005

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.930
and had failed to file
taxes from 2010 to 2015,

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.230
where DMX had made at least 2.3 million.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.890
Pro tip, not legal advice:
always file your taxes,

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.180
especially for a five-year period

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.780
where you're making millions of dollars.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.030
But in November of 2017, DMX
changed his plea to guilty,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.200
and prior to sentencing,
prosecutors were seeking

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.880
the maximum penalty for
five years in prison.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.820
So enter the father-daughter legal team

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.820
of Murray "Don't Worry Murray"
Richman and Stacey Richman

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.980
who decided to try a
novel music-based strategy

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.930
to convince U.S. district
judge Jed Rakoff to be lenient.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.610
At DMX's sentencing hearing,
Murray Richman argued

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.860
that his client suffered
a nightmarish childhood,

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.190
which had led to repeated
encounters with the law

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.960
at an early age and set him
on a bad path as an adult.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.700
To illustrate his point, Murray
requested that Judge Rakoff

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.670
watch his client's music video
for DMX's hit song "Slippin'"

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.210
that lyrically describes
his traumatic upbringing.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.220
Growing up, DMX was
abandoned by his father,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.340
lived in extreme poverty,
endured severe psychological

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.070
and physical abuse from his
mother and her boyfriends

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.590
who knocked out DMX's teeth
and left prominent scars

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.880
on his face as a young boy,

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.220
and then was introduced
to drugs at 14 years old.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.500
Murray argued that watching
this video would show

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.300
how DMX was not a bad person,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.830
just that his difficult upbringing meant

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.060
he was simply not prepared
for the responsibility

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.200
of having lots of money.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.390
The judge agreed to watch the video.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.870
And after listening to the
song, Judge Rakoff remarked

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.520
that in the eyes of the
court, DMX was a good man,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.870
noting, "In many ways,
he's his own worst enemy."

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.230
Judge Rakoff then gave
DMX a reduced sentence

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.490
for one year in prison
and ordered him to pay

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.750
2.3 million in back taxes.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.160
After sentencing DMX, his
co-counsel, Stacey Richman,

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.020
explained the rationale
for playing "Slippin'"

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:17.853
for the court.

00:03:17.853 --> 00:03:19.870
- This was about the
humanity of one person

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.430
reaching out to everyone else,

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.710
and it's not about getting a path, a pass.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.130
It's about getting a path.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.310
- And after learning about this case,

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.600
I'm gonna have to talk to my clients

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.410
about their bizarre lack of hit songs

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.670
to support their cases.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.480
I mean, I can't do all the work for you.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.170
But that brings us to the Twinkie Defense,

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.790
which is a very derisive term

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.360
for a thing that actually happened,

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.520
though it is incredibly misunderstood.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.930
The most common legal strategy
for defending murder suspects

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.580
is to deny all allegations and
force the government to prove

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.400
every factual element of their case.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.730
But when there is no dispute

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.370
that the defendant committed the crime,

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.910
defense counsel will often shift

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.140
to the defendant's mental state

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.550
to show why the defendant
is not legally responsible

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.340
for the crime and at a minimum
deserves a less severe charge

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.430
than first degree murder.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.890
And such as the case with Dan White,

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.240
a former San Francisco city
supervisor who assassinated

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.100
then-Mayor George Moscone
and Supervisor Harvey Milk

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.640
in a rampage at city hall,
turned himself into the police,

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.980
and then confessed to the crime.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.410
- Well, I'm definitely a law and order.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.090
I campaign very hard on
what I consider to be

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.337
the number one priority
not only for my district,

00:04:16.337 --> 00:04:20.470
but for San Francisco, and that
is to make this a safe city.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.410
- Now this has been the
subject of several movies,

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.410
but here's the pertinent
actual background.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.730
On January 8th, 1978, Harvey Milk became

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.590
the first openly gay elected official

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.890
in the history of California.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.580
A fervent advocate for gay rights,

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.960
Milk's first official act on
the board was to introduce

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.150
a bill, which passed almost unanimously,

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.610
outlawing discrimination
based on sexual orientation

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.910
in employment, housing,
and public accommodations.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:43.660
Milk's famously brash
brand of liberal politics

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.090
frequently brought him into conflict

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.550
with that of conservative
fellow supervisor Dan White,

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.180
a 32-year-old former police
officer and firefighter.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.340
For example, White was
the lone dissenting vote

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.600
against Milk's
non-discrimination ordinance.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.850
Tensions between the two
began to reach a boiling point

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.520
when Milk cast the deciding vote

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.130
in favor of opening a halfway
home in White's district

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.310
for troubled adolescents.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.310
White stated that he
felt betrayed by Milk,

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.760
who had initially promised
to oppose a halfway home,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.260
and soon became disillusioned
with the Board of Supervisors.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.640
11 months into his tenure,
White abruptly resigned

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.790
from the board on November 10th, 1978.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.700
White claimed that he could
not support his family

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.890
on a $9,600 salary

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:20.170
and announced that he was
leaving politics for good.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.010
Four days later, in response to pressure

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.040
from conservative-leaning
police and business groups

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.480
who feared that the mayor
would appoint a replacement

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.010
who would create a six-five
liberal-conservative split,

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.970
White sought to withdraw his resignation.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.550
Although Mayor Moscone initially agreed

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.760
to give White his job back,

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.020
the mayor changed course
following an outpouring of outrage

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.930
from White's constituents who blasted him

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.560
as ineffective and inattentive.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.450
On November 27th, 1978, the
mayor was set to appoint

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.650
community activist Don
Horanzy as supervisor.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.120
Angered that his plan to return
to the board was thwarted,

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.710
White then showed up at city hall,

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.210
slipped into a window to
avoid metal detectors,

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.000
and confronted the mayor at his office.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.070
When the mayor refused White's
demand to be reappointed,

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.220
White proceeded to shoot and
kill the mayor execution style.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.810
He then walked down the hall
and murdered Harvey Milk

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.710
as well, murdering his former colleague.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.400
Both Moscone and Milk immediately
died from their injuries.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.610
Soon, then-acting-Mayor Dianne Feinstein

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.280
made the stunning
announcement to the press.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.150
- Both Mayor Moscone and
Supervisor Harvey Milk

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.580
have been shot and killed.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.990
- Oh, Jesus Christ!
- Oh!

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.543
- The suspect is Supervisor Dan White.

00:06:22.543 --> 00:06:25.910
- Later that day, White visited
his former police precinct

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.830
to turn himself in and
confess to the killings

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.460
in a recorded interview.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.360
- [Dan] And then he
started kind of smirking

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.090
'cause he knew, he knew I
wasn't gonna be reappointed.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:39.090
And he just kinda smirked at
me as if to say, "Too bad."

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:44.250
And then I just got all
flushed and hot and I shot him.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.620
- The assassinations roiled
the city of San Francisco,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.719
resulting in an outpouring
of spontaneous support

00:06:48.719 --> 00:06:49.617
and mourning from the community.

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:51.920
And at trial, the
defense counsel for White

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.770
argued that White's longstanding
and untreated depression

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.940
gave him what's called
diminished capacity,

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.530
such that he could not distinguish
between right and wrong,

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.840
and thus lack the required
intent to be found guilty

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.000
of premeditated first degree murder.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.810
Remember that the difference
between first, second,

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.590
and third degree murder usually depends

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.270
on the mental state of the accused.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.540
Dr. Martin Blinder, one of
the five expert witnesses

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.590
called by the defense,
testified in the days

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:14.820
leading up to the killings

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.940
White, known for being
focused on personal health

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:20.610
and fitness, cast aside his
normal habits, grew stubble,

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.940
and in lieu of his normal healthy diet,

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.490
indulged in junk food.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.760
Blinder testified that
White's excessive consumption

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.930
of junk food, including Twinkies,

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:30.790
which were only mentioned in passing,

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.360
where evidence of his depressed state

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.130
that had exacerbated his
already existing depression.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.350
And the jury bought this
diminished capacity defense

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.470
and White was convicted
of voluntary manslaughter

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.010
rather than first degree murder.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:44.270
He served five years in prison
of a seven-year sentence.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.520
Less than two years later,
White returned to San Francisco

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.700
and committed suicide.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.550
Outrage after the verdict led
to a series of violent events

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.710
in San Francisco that would be known

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.300
as the White Night Riots.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.220
And following intense negative publicity,

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.940
in 1982, California abolished
the term diminished capacity

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.000
as a legal defense

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.020
and replaced it with something
called diminished actuality.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.360
Under this new standard,
evidence of mental illness

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.800
is admissible to show a defendant
lacked the specific intent

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.310
to commit the specific crime
in which they were charged,

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.310
as opposed to the prior standard
that could be used to show

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.200
that the defendant lacks all capacity

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.570
to have any specific
intent to commit any crime.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.520
And as you can imagine,
many people were upset

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.230
about the outcome of the White trial,

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.730
which is where the Twinkie
Defense name comes in.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.020
In stories covering the trial,

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.970
San Francisco satirist Paul Krassner

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.650
played up the angle of the Twinkie

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.480
and claims that he may
have even coined the term

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.313
the Twinkie Defense.

00:08:29.313 --> 00:08:30.900
Derisive reporters covering the trial

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.820
seized on the testimony made in passing

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.340
that White had eaten Twinkies

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.180
in the days leading up to the murders,

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.630
adopted the Twinkie Defense framing,

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:41.120
which led to decades of misunderstanding.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.730
And due to this misreporting in the press,

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.460
much of the public erroneously believed

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.680
that White's lawyers
had argued that Twinkies

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.570
drove White to commit the murder.

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.840
In reality, White's lawyers
argued that the junk food

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.130
was a symptom of his diminished
capacity, not the cause.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.530
But this misconception that
White received a lesser charge

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.510
by claiming junk food
made him commit murder,

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.920
which was repeated at the end
of the 2008 biopic "Milk,"

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.260
persists to this day.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.560
Nevertheless, the actual defense advanced

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.860
was still controversial
for successfully reducing

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.080
White's charges from
murder to manslaughter.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.840
Since then, some commentators have argued

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.220
that the so-called Twinkie
Defense was less pivotal

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.170
to White's defense then was the
relatively conservative jury

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.470
who possibly supported and sympathized

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.740
with the former supervisor.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.870
It was reported at the time
that when the jury listened

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.730
to Dan White's recorded murder confession,

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.390
several of them actually wept.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.740
And today the term the Twinkie Defense

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.830
has become a derisive catchall label

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.810
for improbable legal defenses,

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.810
like the ones that we're
talking about in this video.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:36.380
And during the oral argument
in the Supreme Court case

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.580
of U.S. versus Gonzalez-Lopez,

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.160
the late Justice Antonin
Scalia famously referenced

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.740
the Twinkie Defense do
suggest that the right

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:45.640
to select one's own counsel
is perhaps more important

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.200
than the right to have
effective assistance of counsel.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.527
The justice argued that, "I
don't want a competent lawyer.

00:09:50.527 --> 00:09:51.627
"I want a lawyer to get me off.

00:09:51.627 --> 00:09:53.517
"I want a lawyer to invent
the Twinkie Defense.

00:09:53.517 --> 00:09:54.740
"I want to win."

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.210
And now we know why lawyers
get accused of being unethical.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.170
But now let's talk about
one crazy legal hypothetical

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.480
that you'd think you'd
only cover in law school,

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.590
but actually happened in real life.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:08.530
What happens when an
identical twin commits murder?

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:11.300
If, like me, you were
raised on TV in the 1990s,

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.930
then you know that the sure-fire formula

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.160
to ensure wacky hijinks
is to introduce twins

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.430
into any situation,
have them switch places,

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.260
and then let the shenanigans unfold.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.810
Remember those classic
episodes where Tia and Tamara

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.910
switch places so they could take tests?

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.820
Or Mary Kate and Ashley switch places

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:26.970
to get their parents together?

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.810
And who can forget that
time that Zack and Cody

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.120
were arrested for drug
trafficking in Malaysia

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.850
but narrowly escaped the death penalty

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.470
when authorities couldn't tell them apart?

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:35.900
Oh, wait a minute. That's my bad.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.510
That actually wasn't a special episode

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:39.020
of "The Sweet Life of Zack and Cody."

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.340
That was a real case where
twin-based shenanigans

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.960
actually prevented brothers
from being executed.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.200
In 2003, Malaysian authorities arrested

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.150
27-year-old identical twins
Sathis Raj and Sabarish Raj

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.120
for trafficking large amounts
of opium and cannabis,

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.530
which in Malaysia carries
a mandatory penalty

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.760
of death by hanging.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.300
The police had caught one twin red handed

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.500
taking a car load of
drugs to another house,

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:03.120
which only he had the key.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.000
And then shortly thereafter,
the other twin arrived

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.200
and was promptly arrested.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.660
At trial, the judge acknowledged
that the first brother

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.660
who was arrested with
a key was the only one

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.810
with access to the drug house,

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.510
and therefore was the only one the state

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:15.710
could be able to prove was
guilty of drug trafficking

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:16.630
beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.830
The problem?

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.670
Due to the twins' identical features,

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.530
it was impossible for
the arresting officers

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.230
to determine which twin
had been initially arrested

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.080
with a key to the drug house.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.080
So further complicating the case,

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.100
the twins refused to admit to any crimes,

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.530
refused to testify against each other,

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:33.850
and the DNA evidence was inconclusive.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:36.030
Unable to identify the
twin originally arrested

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:39.260
in possession of the drugs,
the judge acquitted both men.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.160
In explaining her decision
to acquit the brothers,

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.058
High Court Judge Zaharah Ibrahim noted,

00:11:43.058 --> 00:11:46.437
"This is a very unique case
as they are identical twins.

00:11:46.437 --> 00:11:48.377
"Even the DNA evidence
could not prove anything

00:11:48.377 --> 00:11:51.347
"as the DNA could be either
Sathis' or Sabarish's.

00:11:51.347 --> 00:11:53.877
"I can't be calling the wrong
twin to enter his defense.

00:11:53.877 --> 00:11:56.270
"I can't be sending the
wrong person to the gallows."

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.240
Or to explain this case using
only "Simpsons" references--

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.900
- He can't kill anybody if he doesn't know

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:04.960
which one's the real Krusty. (grunting)

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:07.260
- Now I would like to tell you
that this case is an outlier

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.820
and that there isn't some identical twin

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:09.920
exception to criming.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.550
Unfortunately, convicting individuals

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:14.760
with identical twin siblings
remains an ongoing dilemma

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:15.730
for law enforcement.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.020
More often than you would think,

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.720
suspects have been acquitted
or have charges dropped

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.440
when authorities can't
prove which twin is guilty.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.640
One problem in these cases
is that eye witnesses

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.800
who struggle to identify the twin

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.370
that committed the actual crime.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:31.230
For example, in 2011,
19-year-old Orlando Nembhard

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.030
was charged with shooting
and killing a man

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.610
outside of an Arizona nightclub.

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:35.760
However, when evidence revealed

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.070
that his twin brother
Brandon was at the scene,

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.610
prosecutors dropped the charges

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.420
when the witnesses were unable to identify

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:42.950
which brother pulled the trigger.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.970
So as you can imagine,
reasonable doubt can be built

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.270
right into these cases.

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:49.880
This isn't a legal issue per
se. It's an evidentiary issue.

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.920
You have to prove your case
beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:54.400
And if you can't identify
which twin it was,

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.580
then you have a pretty uphill climb.

